 "_self_report_instruction_note": "v1.2.0: the ORPHANED self-report instruction verbs (describe/tell/report/explain/say/show/state/list/account/summarise/summarize -- previously only handled by the dead-code Python path domains/conversation_action.act_on_instruction, unreachable from converse()) are re-homed graph-natively: each is a held Concept{instruction_route:'self_report'} below (teach-extensible, like every instruction route -- see comprehend_instruction v2.0.0), and instruction_self_report_identity routes a REFLEXIVE self-report instruction ('describe yourself', 'tell me about yourself' -- the predicate Mention resolves to a self_report route Concept AND a mention resolves to the reflexive 'yourself'/'yourselves' Concept, gap_awareness's held self-words) to the SAME substrate-identity account reply_self_identity speaks, minting Goal{kind:report_self}. DELIBERATELY NARROW: a possessive-object self-report ('show me your gaps', 'list your limitations') is NOT claimed here -- the reflexive-vs-possessive distinction is the same discriminator the topic-route possessive guard uses -- so those turns flow to the unhandled-instruction gap pipeline (gap_awareness v1.6.0) instead of a misleading identity reply. A NON-self self-report instruction ('summarise the report', 'tell me about the moon') has no reflexive mention, is not claimed, and files a gap likewise.",
